=== HINT 1: Writer ===
AcquireSRWLockExclusive(&g_lock);
g_counter++;
WakeAllConditionVariable(&g_cv);
ReleaseSRWLockExclusive(&g_lock);

=== HINT 2: Reader ===
AcquireSRWLockShared(&g_lock);
long val = g_counter;
ReleaseSRWLockShared(&g_lock);
if (val != last) { printf("counter = %ld\n", val); last = val; }

=== HINT 3: SleepConditionVariableSRW (optional improvement) ===
Instead of spinning in the reader loop, sleep on the condition variable:
  AcquireSRWLockShared(&g_lock);
  SleepConditionVariableSRW(&g_cv, &g_lock, 100, CONDITION_VARIABLE_LOCKMODE_SHARED);
  // re-check condition after wake
  ReleaseSRWLockShared(&g_lock);

=== KEY INSIGHT ===
Multiple readers can hold the lock simultaneously (shared).
A writer waits until ALL readers release before it acquires exclusive.
This gives much better read throughput than a plain mutex for read-heavy workloads.
